.TH DVBIPITOOLS 1 "2026-10-19" "dvbipitools" "dvbipitools Manual"
.SH NAME
dvbipitools \- multicall binary bundling every dvbipitools tool

.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBdvbipitools\f1 \fItool\fR [\fIargs\fR ...]
.br
\fBdipi\f1 \fIshort\-name\fR [\fIargs\fR ...]
.br
\fItool\fR [\fIargs\fR ...]
.br
\fBdvbipitools\f1 \-\-list
.br
\fBdvbipitools\f1 \-\-install [\fB\-h\fR] \fIDIR\fR
.br
\fBdvbipitools\f1 \-\-version

.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBdvbipitools\f1 is one executable containing every tool/daemon in this project:
\fBdipibcg\fR, \fBdipibim\fR, \fBdipicam378\fR, \fBdipidescramble\fR,
\fBdipifccret\fR, \fBdipimetrics\fR, \fBdipiradiohead\fR, \fBdipirec\fR,
\fBdipirist\fR, \fBdipiscan\fR, \fBdipisds\fR, \fBdipisrt\fR,
\fBdipitvhead\fR, \fBdipixmltv\fR, \fBdipixy\fR.
.br

Three ways to call it:

.TP
.B By full tool name
\fBdvbipitools\fR \fItool\fR [\fIargs\fR ...], e.g. \fBdvbipitools dipiscan \-h\fR.
.TP
.B By short name
\fBdipi\fR \fIshort\-name\fR [\fIargs\fR ...], where \fIshort\-name\fR drops
the \fBdipi\fR prefix, e.g. \fBdipi scan \-h\fR. Both entry points accept
either the full or the short name.
.TP
.B By symlink or hardlink
Linking \fBdvbipitools\fR under any tool's own name, e.g.  \fIdipiscan\f1 \-> \fBdvbipitools\fR.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-list
Print the name of every applet.
.TP
\fB\-\-install\fR [\fB\-h\fR] \fIDIR\fR
Create a symlink per applet in \fIDIR\fR, each pointing to the
absolute path of the running binary. \fB \-h \f1 creates hardlinks.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH APPLETS
Full name and short name (for the
.B dipi
entry point):
.PP
.RS
dipibcg          bcg
.br
dipibim          bim
.br
dipicam378       cam378
.br
dipidescramble   descramble
.br
dipifccret       fccret
.br
dipimetrics      metrics
.br
dipiradiohead    radiohead
.br
dipirec          rec
.br
dipirist         rist
.br
dipiscan         scan
.br
dipisds          sds
.br
dipisrt          srt
.br
dipitvhead       tvhead
.br
dipixmltv        xmltv
.br
dipixy           xy
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B dvbipitools dipiscan \-m 239.19.75.0 >hd.m3u
Run \fBdipiscan\fR by its full name.
.TP
.B dipi scan \-m 239.19.75.0 >hd.m3u
Same, via the short form.
.TP
.B ln \-s dvbipitools dipirec && ./dipirec \-i ... \-o ...
Run \fBdipirec\fR via a symlink to \fBdvbipitools\fR.
.TP
.B dvbipitools \-\-install /usr/local/bin
Symlink every applet at \fI/usr/local/bin\fR.
.TP
.B dvbipitools \-\-install \-h /opt/dipi
(hardlinks)
